    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #298\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-204-mail-sync-hardening-04-04-converge-pro-thr_yj4w7urecm` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis closes out issue #204: `ingestEmailMessage` no longer surfaces a raw Postgres unique-violation when two sync passes race to ingest distinct Message-IDs that turn out to share the same `provider_message_id`.\n\n- `backend/packages/data/src/mail/mailMessageMetaStore.ts`: added `isProviderMessageIdConflict`, recognizing a `23505` violation specifically on the existing partial unique index `mail_message_meta_provider_msg_uq`.\n- `backend/packages/data/src/mail/ingest.ts`: the \"new message\" branch now runs under a `SAVEPOINT`; on a provider-id conflict it rolls back the loser's item/thread/meta writes and converges onto the winning row's existing item identity instead of throwing, then still links the folder relation so synchronization continues.\n- No migration needed — the partial unique index already existed; the gap was only in application-layer conflict handling.\n- Added tests covering: concurrent distinct messages sharing one provider id converging to a single stable row with no raw error, the pre-existing same-message-id fill via `ON CONFLICT (message_id) DO UPDATE`, and the null-provider-id message-id-only path.\n- Full verification: `tsc --noEmit` clean, and `vitest run` passes all 24 test files / 316 tests.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
